# Exam track — Theme: Hobbien & Fräizäit — Sub-lesson 2: Key Phrases
# Plain sentences (no @question): presented in either direction.
# Mixed with the vocabulary these phrases lean on, so sessions alternate
# word-match and sentence-builder slots. Grounded in the user's real hobbies
# (photography, hiking, rock music, dance, dioramas) rather than generic
# statements — see .claude/memory/exam-track.md on why topic content should
# stay personal even outside the @question file.
#
# Three sentences here are @fill rather than @sentence: their word order carried
# more decisions than a learner can hold as loose tiles (V2 after a time
# adverbial, a perfect bracket, a modal bracket).
#
# Distractors are deliberately FORM distractors — wrong tense, wrong person, wrong
# auxiliary, wrong inflection of the right lemma. The prompt shows the complete
# English sentence, so the MEANING is already given and a distractor that differs
# only in meaning (`Kamera` where the prompt says "material") is eliminable by
# vocabulary alone and tests nothing. What the learner must still choose is the
# correct form, which is exactly what the exam marks.
# See .claude/memory/fill-in-words-exercise.md § Second purpose.

@lesson H1.02 "Hobbies Phrases"

@word wanderen = to hike
@word de Bierg = the mountain
@word fotografeieren = to take photographs
@word d'Fotografie = photography
@word d'Kamera = the camera
@word d'Landschaft = the landscape
@word de Concert = the concert
@word d'Rockmusek = rock music
@word d'Instrument = the instrument
@word de Sport = the sport
@word spillen = to play
@word dobaussen = outdoors
@word de Fotoapparat = the camera (apparatus)
@word d'Diorama = the diorama
@word d'Miniatur = the miniature
@word d'Duerf = the village
@word bauen = to build
@word d'Material = the material

@fill
@lu Am Summer [wanderen] ech gär [dobaussen], an ech [ginn] oft op de Bierg.
@en In summer I like [hiking] [outdoors], and I often [go] up the mountain.
@distractor-lu wandert
@distractor-lu doheem
@distractor-lu geet
@distractor-en hikes
@distractor-en at home
@distractor-en goes

@sentence
@lu Ech fotografeiere gär d'Landschaft mat menger Kamera.
@en I like photographing the landscape with my camera.
@distractor-lu Musek
@distractor-lu Concert
@distractor-en music
@distractor-en concert

@sentence
@lu Ech lauschtere gär Rockmusek, an ech ginn heiansdo op e Concert.
@en I like listening to rock music, and I sometimes go to a concert.
@distractor-lu Sport
@distractor-lu Instrument
@distractor-en sport
@distractor-en instrument

@fill
@lu Ech [hu] wéi [Kand] gär [gedanzt], mee haut spillen ech kee Instrument.
@en As a [child] I [liked] [dancing], but today I don't play an instrument.
@distractor-lu sinn
@distractor-lu Kanner
@distractor-lu danzen
@distractor-en am
@distractor-en children
@distractor-en dance

@sentence
@lu Ech reparéiere gär Saachen a menger neier Wunneng.
@en I like repairing things in my new apartment.
@distractor-lu Kamera
@distractor-lu Musek
@distractor-en camera
@distractor-en music

@sentence
@lu Wann ech Zäit hunn, liesen ech gär e Buch.
@en When I have time, I like reading a book.
@distractor-lu reent
@distractor-lu Stad
@distractor-en rains
@distractor-en city

@sentence
@lu Ech géif gär Miniature vun Dierfer bauen.
@en I would like to build miniatures of villages.
@distractor-lu Musek
@distractor-lu Sport
@distractor-en music
@distractor-en sport

@sentence
@lu Mäi Papp hat e Fotoapparat, an ech maachen och gär Fotoen.
@en My father had a camera, and I also like taking photos.
@distractor-lu Instrument
@distractor-lu Concert
@distractor-en instrument
@distractor-en concert

@sentence
@lu D'nächst Joer wëll ech op Norwegen fueren.
@en Next year I want to go to Norway.
@distractor-lu Musek
@distractor-lu Bicher
@distractor-en music
@distractor-en books

@fill
@lu Ech [hu] scho Material fir Diorama doheem, mee ech [muss] nach Zäit [fannen].
@en I already [have] material for dioramas at home, but I still [need] to [find] time.
@distractor-lu sinn
@distractor-lu mussen
@distractor-lu fonnt
@distractor-en am
@distractor-en needs
@distractor-en found
